{
  "generatedAt": "2026-09-02",
  "computedNotMeasured": "The memory figures are computed, not benchmarked. Weights are the parameter count times bytes per weight; the KV cache is 2 x layers x key_value_heads x head_dim x context x bytes; a fixed runtime allowance is added. The architecture fields they are computed from come from each model config.json and are not estimates.",
  "formula": {
    "weightsBytes": "parameters * bits_per_weight / 8",
    "kvCacheBytes": "2 * layers * key_value_heads * head_dim * context * kv_bytes",
    "runtimeOverheadGb": 0.8,
    "note": "key_value_heads, not attention_heads. Grouped-query attention shares one key-value pair across several query heads, so using the query head count overstates the cache by the gqa_ratio — up to eightfold in this dataset. It is the commonest error in VRAM estimates."
  },
  "caveats": {
    "slidingWindow": "Not modelled. Gemma 2 alternates local and global attention layers, so its real cache at long context is smaller than shown. The figures for those models are an upper bound.",
    "usableFraction": "assumed_usable_gb is an assumption about how much memory a model can actually occupy, not a measured value. Discrete cards are assumed to keep 8% back for the driver and display; Apple Silicon follows the documented macOS cap on what one process may take.",
    "quantisation": "GGUF K-quants are not their nominal bit width. Q4_K_M averages about 4.5 bits per weight once block scales and higher-precision attention tensors are counted, so files are roughly 12% larger than \"4-bit\" implies."
  },
